    "body": "- [ ] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nFail explicitly when routing-map padding cannot reach the requested alignment within the existing token capacity.\n\nFor example, an expert receiving 90 of 100 tokens cannot be padded to a multiple of 128 by flipping existing zero entries. Both helpers previously returned 100 tokens for that expert without reporting that the alignment contract was not met.\n\n- Check that each expert's next aligned token count fits within `num_tokens` in both `pad_routing_map` and `fused_pad_routing_map`.\n- Use `torch._assert_async` to avoid adding a device-to-host synchronization on the CUDA path. Infeasible CPU inputs raise `RuntimeError`; on CUDA the assertion is asynchronous and may surface at a later synchronization point.\n- Document the capacity precondition and add three CPU tensor regression cases for normal padding, the exact-capacity boundary, and the reported infeasible input.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nFixes #6086.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe three new tests are in `tests/unit_tests/transformer/moe/test_token_dispatcher.py`:\n\n- `test_pad_routing_map_pads_each_expert_to_multiple`\n- `test_pad_routing_map_uses_every_remaining_token_when_needed`\n- `test_pad_routing_map_raises_when_not_enough_tokens`\n\nThe CPU regression cases were not rerun for this submission. CUDA/Triton execution, fused/non-fused GPU parity, functional tests, and the complete repository test suite have not been verified for this submission.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n### Pre-checks\n\n- [x] I have added relevant unit tests\n- [ ] I have added relevant functional tests\n- [ ] If this PR adds or changes a GPU kernel (Triton, `jit_fuser`/`torch.compile`, CUDA extension, TE or external-library dispatch, or a scatter/index accumulation), I have added or updated its bit-exact determinism test and registered it in `tests/unit_tests/determinism/kernels/manifest.py`\n- [x] I have added proper typing to my code (existing typed helper signatures are unchanged)\n- [x] I have added relevant documentation (helper docstrings)\n- [ ] I have run the `tools/autoformat.sh` on my PR\n\n### Draft review notes\n\n- The PR author's personal line-by-line review attestation remains unchecked pending the author's own review.\n- Both changed helpers are registered kernel sources, but this branch does not update their determinism replay tests. The repository's kernel-coverage check is expected to require corresponding test updates before review.\n- The existing commit includes a `Signed-off-by` trailer but is not cryptographically signed.\n\nThis PR starts as a draft in accordance with the contribution process.\n",
